#
# Counter-example for the cross-node-glut rule: two opposing-polarity findings that
# share an anchor which is NOT typed gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor (the shared empty /
# default anchor locationless findings collapse onto). The gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor
# guard keeps the join off the placeholder, so the rule must derive NO
# gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith even though the polarities oppose and the anchor is
# shared. This is the load-bearing guard against false-joining locationless
# findings. Consumed ONLY by
# crates/conformance/tests/diagnostics_meta_findings.rs; lives under tests/ so the
# global make validate gate never loads it as data.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/diagnostics/tests/> .

# NOTE: ex:taAnchor is deliberately NOT typed gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor.
ex:taA
    a gmeow:Finding ;
    gmeow:findingAnchor ex:taAnchor ;
    gmeow:findingCategory logic:FindingContradictionWitness .

ex:taB
    a gmeow:Finding ;
    gmeow:findingAnchor ex:taAnchor ;
    gmeow:findingCategory logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict .
